[Music]  okay everyone this is my spoiler review  of the new predator prequel pray  this was directed by dan trattenberg and  written by patrick iason it stars amber  mid thunder so  with this film i had low expectations  because i was someone in the camp that  wasn't crazy about 10 cloverfield lane  the previous film that dan trachtenberg  had directed and i was prepping for this  film by re-watching the first predator  to get me kind of in the mindset about  just the lore and everything that comes  with it and i was pleasantly surprised  how great this film was  there was a lot of things i liked about  this film and  what this film did so well was have such  a great idea where it was going to go  from point a to point b and on the way  there everything had a purpose and the  amount of action you got for a film when  you want to see an awesome villain like  predator in it you got that payoff in  the original unique ways that weren't  seen in previous films and it felt fresh  enough but thematically the way we  follow this character of nauru and what  was great about nauru is that she starts  off as someone who is struggling and  she's weak and becomes strong as the  film moves on and becomes what she wants  to be by the end but learns as well and  that it's not exactly what she wanted in  the end but she got it what she needed  in the sense of becoming this  hunter this predator  but in the way her brother had taught  her where it was about not just hunting  to hunt it was hunting to survive and  she does that here by the end protecting  her tribe and getting the big prey which  was the predator but also the best part  of this film was just the line her  talking about what makes her so  dangerous is not being seen as a threat  which was perfectly thematic for the  predator because the predator is so  dangerous because he  sees people as threats he detects them  and to have that is such a skill and  something to embrace for the character  of  nauru was awesome and it works so well  here and even getting to see naoru do  really badass things when she gets these  trappers and actually takes him down a  lot like the predator himself and it was  cool to kind of warm us up to things  where we saw the predator taking out  predator animals that were after their  prey but it would come around full  circle by nauru making the predator her  prey and her becoming a predator i also  love things they showed here about  humanity where it's thrown in there but  you gotta catch it that when she finds  that skinned water buffalo we know  that's not the predator who did that  that was human beings the trappers which  speaks a lot about humanity and the  predators we can be because the water  buffalo are non-threatening animals so  it really came full circle in that sense  it's little things like that that made  this film special and little moments  visually too where when she's first  going on the hunt by herself her walking  past all the woman that are in their  usual roles just gathering things  walking the other direction but she's  walking opposite them that visually  spoke so much which was great and just  as a fan of the character of the  predator cool little things we got to  see him actually  making his skull here of the wolf that  was cool because we know he keeps those  as collectibles and i love when we saw  the predator versus the bear it was a  cool way for nauru to first see the  predator but just the fight was pretty  intense and having the bear  just having the predator's blood come  out of his mouth was really sick and it  had a lot of revenant vibes and i love  the scene when the predator attacks the  jerks that are in naaru's tribe  but it seemed a lot like the original  predator sequence where they have guns  but this time they replaced the guns  with bows so i thought that was really  effective and even things that are set  up in the beginning that come full  circle like having a point to the moment  where the dog has his tail caught in the  trap  to have naru eventually get caught by  that same trap later on was brilliant  and i like the brother got a line here  saying if it bleeds we can kill it  that's just a shout out to the first  film directly from the first film that  line and man when the predator has this  big showdown jumping from tree to tree  in this fog that was so cool and him  using the net to devour that guy and  then one he throws a bear trap to the  head and even humor here of the trappers  having to reload their guns because it's  taking place in the olden days i thought  was actually great and it was sick what  they did with this predator because he  has this awesome shield it kind of  actually felt like wonder woman a bit  that sequence in the fog when he's using  it but like i said it switched things up  and it was brutal they didn't get soft  with the predator and they didn't wait  too long to have him doing these awesome  brutal kills that's what we want to see  and i thought they were all creative and  excellent and it was nice that the  brother wasn't just thrown away and made  a jerk like he had his faults too but he  ended up giving great guidance to his  sister in the end and learning himself  and  saving the dog in the end and goes out  of champ which was awesome and we get a  great final payoff scene with nauru vs  predator and her learning all these  smart ways about the predator how to  stop him and killing him in a smart way  not just some easy way of strength it  was of  wits and brilliance and  i love she got this big victory cry at  the end when she beat him as we all felt  it was cool they got the dog involved  too the dog was a great side character  for nauru and it was a great performance  by amber mid thunder you're seeing a  star in the making here so it's actually  just something that if you're looking at  a film that's this  suspenseful and intense and is simple  but not simple meaning there's a lot of  themes here and it kept me invested the  whole time but you're also getting great  action here everything is creative and  thought outside the box you can tell  there's a lot of work put into this and  the beautiful visuals the environment  the setting it was in i couldn't have  imagined a better case scenario for this  film that it was just a great prequel to  a franchise that's really been dead in  the water so i'm really impressed this  is the shocker of the year for me how  good this was  and i  really am just  appalled that they didn't release this  in theaters it's a head scratcher that  they just put this straight to hulu i  would have loved to watch this in  theaters and i think it would have done  really well because of the praise it's  getting from critics and fans and that  it's still part of a franchise people  know and are familiar with so i think it  would have done good so it's strange it  didn't release it in theaters but i hope  people keep talking about and watch this  this is one of the best  just thriller survivor films i've seen  in a long time i'm giving this one a 9.2  i think it's even better than the  original that's not recency bias just  watching them back to back this is a  better film hands down it doesn't have  any cheesiness here it's great acting  great action great themes and again  everything's serving a purpose with a  pace that moves brisk and doesn't feel  slow at all so and again great visuals  too so i think it just justifies  existence and even more and to top the  original in my eyes is just amazing i am  so shocked how good this film was so i'm  excited and it gets me hyped again for  future films that might be in this  franchise with a predator and we can  stay with this character of nauru and  have new threats of different predators  and kind of maybe lead into the original  predator film i'm excited to see where  they go with this and even they hinted  at predator 2 here with the gun at the  end that we saw in that film here at the  end so really you know the